  content = '# UPPSC Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination Notification 2026: Vacancies, Online Form, Dates & Gazette PDF\n\n> **Official Gazette Verification**: This dossier is verified against official gazette notification issued by **UPPSC** under Advt Ref: **A-1/E-1/2026**.  \n> **Recruitment Cadre**: UP | **Academic & Recruitment Cycle**: 2026 | **Authority Status**: Active Official Recruitment\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ Executive Notification Fact Sheet\n\n| Key Parameter | Official Verified Detail |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Recruiting Authority** | **UPPSC** |\n| **Recruitment Notice Title** | **Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination** |\n| **Official Advertisement Ref** | **A-1/E-1/2026** |\n| **Total Sanctioned Vacancies** | **1,000 Posts** |\n| **Prescribed Educational Level** | **Graduate Degree in any discipline from a recognized University** |\n| **Sanctioned Pay Structure** | **Pay Matrix Level 4 to Level 8 (₹25,500 - ₹1,51,100)** |\n| **Online Application Start Date** | **01 January 2026** |\n| **Last Date to Apply Online** | **28 January 2026** |\n| **Tentative Examination Date** | **18 October 2026** |\n| **Application Submission Mode** | Exclusively Online |\n| **Official Direct Portal** | [UPPSC Official Apply Portal](https://uppsc.up.nic.in) |\n\n---\n\n## 📌 1. Administrative Scope & Notification Mandate\n\nThe **UPPSC** has officially released notification **A-1/E-1/2026** announcing **1,000 vacancies** for **Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination**. This competitive recruitment cycle is enacted under statutory civil service and cadre management rules to induct qualified personnel into national and regional departments.\n\nThe selection mechanism enforces a merit-driven, multi-tier evaluation comprising Computer-Based Examinations (CBT), departmental skill tests where mandated, and comprehensive biometric document verification. Given the competitive nature of UPPSC recruitments, candidates must adhere strictly to the published gazette guidelines to ensure their candidature remains valid throughout the recruitment cycle.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 2. Category-Wise Vacancy & Horizontal Reservation Matrix\n\nSanctioned vacancies are categorized according to constitutional reservation policies established by the Government of India. The tentative breakdown across administrative quotas is structured as follows:\n\n| Category / Quota | Distribution Status | Reservation Percentage | Remarks |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Unreserved (General / UR)** | Open Merit Allocation | ~40.5% | Open to all qualifying candidates across India |\n| **Other Backward Classes (OBC-NCL)**| Non-Creamy Layer | 27.0% | Valid Central NCL certificate mandated |\n| **Economically Weaker Sections (EWS)**| Income & Asset Criterion | 10.0% | Certificate issued for financial year 2025-2026 |\n| **Scheduled Castes (SC)** | Statutory Quota | 15.0% | Central Government certificate format |\n| **Scheduled Tribes (ST)** | Statutory Quota | 7.5% | Prescribed competent authority endorsement |\n| **PwD / Divyangjan** | Horizontal Reservation | 4.0% | Minimum 40% benchmark disability required |\n| **Ex-Servicemen (ESM)** | Horizontal Reservation | As per cadre rules | Army / Navy / Air Force discharge verification |\n\n*Note: Vacancy figures are provisional and subject to minor administrative revisions prior to the declaration of final merit lists.*\n\n---\n\n## 📅 3. Comprehensive Timeline & Milestone Calendar\n\nTo prevent deadline defaults, aspirants should track the critical examination milestones:\n\n- **Official Gazette Publication Date**: Available and cataloged on the UPPSC official server.\n- **Online Registration Commencement**: **01 January 2026**.\n- **Closing Date for Online Form Submission**: **28 January 2026 (23:59 IST)**.\n- **Last Date for Online Fee Settlement**: Typically 24 hours following the registration closure.\n- **Application Correction Window**: Commission will provide a dedicated 3-day correction facility for demographic edits.\n- **City Intimation Slip & Admit Card Release**: Scheduled 7 to 10 days before the preliminary test on [HamariJobs Admit Cards Hub](https://hamarijobs.com/admit-cards).\n- **Scheduled Examination Window**: **18 October 2026**.\n- **Provisional Answer Key Release**: Expected within 5 to 7 days post-examination on [HamariJobs Results Portal](https://hamarijobs.com/results).\n\n---\n\n## 💳 4. Application Fee Schedule & Payment Modes\n\nThe fee structure established for **Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination** is outlined below:\n\n| Candidate Category | Prescribed Fee | Processing Charges | Permissible Payment Modes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **General / OBC / EWS (Male)** | **General / OBC / EWS: ₹100** | Nil (Included) | Net Banking, UPI (BHIM/GPay), Visa/Mastercard Debit/Credit |\n| **SC / ST / PwD Candidates** | **Exempted (₹0)** | Nil | Direct exemption applied upon category selection |\n| **All Female Candidates** | **Exempted (₹0)** | Nil | Direct gender exemption applicable |\n| **Ex-Servicemen (ESM)** | **Exempted / Nominal** | Nil | As per Department of Personnel & Training (DoPT) rules |\n\n*Crucial Directive: Application fees paid via unauthorized offline bank challans without official transaction validation will result in the immediate cancellation of candidature.*\n\n---\n\n## 📝 5. Step-by-Step Online Application Protocol\n\nCandidates must follow this standardized sequence to avoid form rejection:\n\n1. **One-Time Registration (OTR)**: Navigate to the official portal at [https://uppsc.up.nic.in](https://uppsc.up.nic.in). Enter candidate legal name, father\'s name, matriculation roll number, active mobile number, and verified email address.\n2. **Profile Creation & Credentials**: Record your generated Registration ID and secure password sent via SMS and email.\n3. **Application Form Population**: Select **Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination 2026** from active notifications. Fill in educational credentials, state preferences, exam center choices, and demographic data.\n4. **Scanned Asset Upload**:\n   - *Photograph*: Color passport image taken against a white background, size 20 KB to 50 KB in JPG/JPEG format. Spectacles and caps are strictly prohibited.\n   - *Signature*: Running hand signature in black ink, size 10 KB to 20 KB.\n5. **Form Preview & Error Verification**: Cross-verify every field against original 10th/12th marksheets. Names must match identity proofs exactly.\n6. **Fee Payment & Final Submission**: Complete transaction through the secure payment gateway. Print the final acknowledgment receipt with the system-generated barcode.\n\n---\n\n## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\n\n### What is the official advertisement number for UPPSC Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination 2026?\nThe official notification has been promulgated under advertisement reference **A-1/E-1/2026** by **UPPSC**.\n\n### How many total vacancies are announced in UPPSC Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination?\nA total of **1,000 posts** have been officially sanctioned. Category-wise vertical and horizontal quotas are detailed in the breakdown table above.\n\n### What is the closing date to apply online for Combined State / Upper Subordinate Services (PCS) Examination?\nThe final deadline to complete online registration and submit applications is **28 January 2026**. Candidates are advised to apply early to avoid server traffic.\n\n### Where can I find the direct official application portal?\nApplications must be submitted exclusively via the official commission portal at [https://uppsc.up.nic.in](https://uppsc.up.nic.in).\n\n### Can candidates edit their application form after submission?\nYes, UPPSC provides an official 2 to 3 day Application Correction Window following registration closure, allowing corrections for a designated administrative fee.',
  status = 'Published',
  updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 69;

